    "humanReview": "Qualitative user approval; numeric ratings remain unmeasured.",
    "entrance": "Eastern side of the long recoil plate.",
    "exit": "Western phase balcony above a thorn field.",
    "solution": "Hold Down until the plate sinks and the tally sits beside the blade under the eaves. Dash Right, then Strike during the outward slide: the dash shades the live beam and creates the opposite shore. At the visible right wall, hold Left and press Jump, including just after the burst ends, to reverse that dash into a super with the rising floor's lift. The high westward arc reaches the opposite landing; another dash switches that landing off.",
    "nearestExisting": "F31 makes a low reverse cut across spent ground. This room instead makes compression solve access to a low target, then uses that same stored displacement for a high return. F35 sends away a lantern weight; here the knight alone controls the spring and the single phase change must be kept.",
    "novelty": "The temporary low position is needed for the outward cut, while the returning lift is needed for the high exit. The new reverse super joins both purposes without a second phase-changing dash.",
    "designNotes": "The broad plate continues supporting the knight at the visible right wall. The shared survive-2 reverse grace now remains available on that original support until a new landing or unrelated state change. The canonical return is genuinely late. Compression has no deadline and Strike can follow Dash rather than requiring a simultaneous chord. Geometry and phase state enforce the puzzle; there is no named-tech exit condition.",
